From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xfree86: define ddxInputThreadInit without an input thread

os.h declares ddxInputThreadInit() for every build, so sdksyms.c lists it
among the symbols modules may use, but xf86Init.c defined it only with
an input thread: --disable-input-thread failed to link Xorg.  It is
defined either way now, empty without the thread.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: N/A the autotools build, which upstream has since replaced
---
--- a/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Init.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Init.c
@@ -1343,12 +1343,12 @@
 }
 #endif
 
-#if INPUTTHREAD
 /** This function is called in Xserver/os/inputthread.c when starting
-    the input thread. */
+    the input thread.  It is part of the module ABI either way. */
 void
 ddxInputThreadInit(void)
 {
+#if INPUTTHREAD
     xf86OSInputThreadInit();
-}
 #endif
+}
